+# Final review: cluster 17 (tests), epic hg-k4l
+
+Invocation inv-17c351e9-bb55-40c3-8436-8b30e7f45319. Source: base 0dbe4772f4cd541e6b5ecaa1dd55b9a72f62c784, head efc21b65eb225578d3a623b29f23b3688849ea8b (both verified with `git rev-parse --verify <sha>^{commit}`). The caller checkout was at efc21b6 with a clean status for the whole review. Source binding to the ledger succeeded.
+
+## Scope
+
+Slices 000080-000086: tests/daemon_composed.rs, tests/daemon_error_commands.rs (new), tests/daemon_free_reads.rs (new), tests/integration_sweep.rs, tests/node_manager_warning.rs (new), tests/seat_exit_codes.rs (new), tests/writer_concurrency.rs. Spec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-05-seat-failure-manager-seats/2026-11-05-seat-failure-manager-seats-design.md at head, which includes a Requirement baseline (B1-B14, S1).
+
+## Analysis
+
+The new integration tests spawn the real binary under `TestRoot` (env_clear plus scrubbed env, process sweep on drop). That meets the global constraint that tests which spawn processes use TestRoot or PrivateHerdr.
+
+tests/seat_exit_codes.rs covers spec §4.4 for `seat`. A dead `HERDR_SOCKET_PATH` gives exit 5, the unavailable prefix, `RETRY_LATER` and the seat-only "Do not guess your seat." sentence, in both text and `--json` forms. With no instance the exit is 2. With HERDR_SOCKET_PATH unset the exit is 2 and stderr is exactly `NOT_IN_HERDR` with no retry text. All of it is traced to production: `seat_failure` in src/cli/seat.rs composes the extra sentences on top of `daemon_error::classify`, which matches the spec rule "composing them with the generic mapping, not through a mode flag".
+
+tests/daemon_error_commands.rs covers §4.4 for the other daemon-calling commands `plan`, `apply` and `writer resume`. Each gets exit 5 with the generic text and without the seat sentences. Production path: `plan_flow`, `apply` (src/cli/plan.rs) and `writer.resume` (src/cli/status.rs:39) all call `daemon_error::report`. With the env value `user-relay`, `apply` reaches the daemon call before failing, so the test exercises the helper and not the confirmation bail-out.
+
+tests/daemon_free_reads.rs covers B14 / §4.13 across who, ops (list and `--unresolved`), op, check-instruction, request list (plain and `--pending`), and undo (`--list` and `--json`). Each command exits 5 with empty stdout and starts no daemon socket. The tests also check that `status` keeps its direct read ("not running", exit 0), and that a read outside Herdr exits 2 with `NOT_IN_HERDR`. Production: who.rs uses `CallMode::NoEnsure` and then `daemon_error::report`. ops.rs, request.rs and undo.rs route through `daemon_error::report`. The only remaining `ClientError::Unavailable` arm in src/cli outside daemon_error.rs is in status.rs:83, the documented exception. The task-5 report records a RED run (fallback returned 0) before GREEN, so the test fails against the old fallback and is not vacuous.
+
+tests/node_manager_warning.rs covers B12 / §4.10 with git2-built instances and no daemon:
+- An unassigned graph with a live seat warns exactly once on stderr, stdout stays clean, and setting `node_manager_seat` silences the warning without changing stdout.
+- An empty graph does not warn.
+- A dangling node manager warns.
+- A retired node manager warns while another seat is live.
+- `seat --hook-prompt`, `init` and the no-instance case do not warn.
+
+Production entry: `node_manager_warning::warn(&cli.command)` at src/cli/mod.rs:88, before dispatch. Its skip list (`Init | Setup | Daemon | seat --hook-prompt`) matches the spec. `setup` and `daemon` are exempted only at parse level, by the unit test `applies_skips_init_setup_daemon_hook_prompt`.
+
+tests/integration_sweep.rs adds `ManagerEdit` and `NodeManagerSet` to the exhaustive `sweep_every_request_kind_has_a_mutation` list and to its no-wildcard match. That proves both kinds have registered writer mutations in `mutation_registry`, the production composition. tests/daemon_composed.rs adds only `node_manager_set` to `ORG_KINDS`, not `manager_edit`. The task-11 report predicted a hg-k4l.13 merge conflict on this list, and the entry appears to have been lost there. Coverage is not lost, because the sweep test is exhaustive over `RequestKind`. tests/writer_concurrency.rs only adds the new `default_manager: None` / `manager: None` record fields, which is mechanical.
+
+Requirement-baseline tracing within this cluster: B1, B2 and B3 (no fallback, retry-later text, carry on) and B14 run from the real CLI entry points through `cli::daemon_error`. B12 runs from `cli::run` through `node_manager_warning::warn`. B4 (exit 6 integrity) has no spawned-binary test in this cluster; it rests on `classify` and `seat_failure` unit tests and on `show`'s `store_failure` path. That path leaves this cluster and is the seam reviewer's to trace. No baseline row this cluster claims is undelivered.
+
+Execution: this review did not rebuild or run these tests at the integrated head. A build needs the ht-build toolbox and the libz shim, and the caller target dir holds no test executables built at efc21b6. The pass evidence comes from the task reports at their task heads: task-2 (seat_exit_codes 3 passed), task-5 (daemon_free_reads 3 passed after RED), task-6 (daemon_error_commands 3 passed after RED), task-14 (node_manager_warning 5 passed), and task-11 (sweep and every_kind_and_command_registered ok). The epic's end-of-run full `cargo test` is the integrated check.
+
+## Findings
+
+- tests/daemon_composed.rs `ORG_KINDS` lists `node_manager_set` but not `manager_edit`, apparently dropped when the hg-k4l.6 and hg-k4l.13 list edits merged. `every_kind_and_command_registered` therefore does not assert the ManagerEdit mutation. No coverage is lost, because `sweep_every_request_kind_has_a_mutation` in tests/integration_sweep.rs asserts it exhaustively.
+- The tests/seat_exit_codes.rs and tests/daemon_error_commands.rs fixtures bind a `UnixListener` at `root.herdr_socket()` and drain it on a thread. Every test then overrides `HERDR_SOCKET_PATH` to a nonexistent `dead.sock` or removes it, so the listener is never contacted. This is dead fixture code that suggests a "reachable Herdr" setup the tests do not actually use.
+- tests/daemon_free_reads.rs `assert!(!f.sock_exists())` is a weak guard that these reads use NoEnsure. An Ensure-mode read would also leave no socket here, because the spawned daemon cannot reach the unbound Herdr socket. The exit-5 assertion, which is the requirement, is unaffected.
+- tests/node_manager_warning.rs `assert!(stdout(&before).contains("s"))` is near-vacuous. It was already recorded as a task-14 deferred minor. The later `assert_eq!(stdout(&after), stdout(&before))` carries the real stdout-stability check.
+
+## Concerns
+
+- The new integration tests were not re-run by this review at efc21b6. Their pass status at the integrated head depends on the epic's final full-suite run.
+
+## Verdict
+ready
+
+## Must fix before landing
+- none
