+## Untested scope
+- Exit 6 (graph integrity) has no spawned-binary test for `seat` or for any other command; it is covered only by `classify`/`seat_failure` unit tests in src/cli (spec §4.4 row "graph integrity").
+- No spawned-binary test covers a hung daemon (read timeout to Frame) or a still-starting daemon (`Remote{Unavailable}`), which spec §4.4 lists as rows to cover; they rest on daemon_error unit tests.
+- Exit 5 is not exercised for the mutating daemon commands `ops cancel`, `ops reassign`, `request ack`, `request complete` and `undo` apply (already a task-5 deferred minor).
+- No end-to-end integration test covers daemon-backed `who` output with the manager line (B9), or `show` exit 6 on a chain integrity failure (already a task-10 deferred minor).
+- The node-manager warning is tested end to end only via `list seats`; the `setup` and `daemon` exemptions and the "any read failure prints nothing" rule (§4.10) are checked only at parse or unit level.
+
